From: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk: fix NETSYS v2 FOE ABI, DSA/EXT routing, RSS, QDMA64 SER, and debugfs bounds

Fix six proven defects affecting NETSYS v2 (MT7981/MT7986):
1. Guard V3-only tail fields in struct hnat_ipv6_hnapt (and keep V2 winfo at offset 82)
   so sizeof(struct foe_entry) matches hardware ABI: 80 B (V1), 96 B (V2), 128 B (V3).
   Wrap V3 new_ipv6_ip* access in foe_extract_dip_v6() accordingly.
2. Clamp default DEF_ETRY_NUM to 16384 (TABLE_16K) on non-V3 targets so NETSYS v2's
   14-bit RXD4 FOE index never overflows.
3. Match DSA LAN/WAN netdevs (IS_DSA_LAN/IS_DSA_WAN) in IS_LAN/IS_WAN so 1-GMAC and
   hybrid DSA MT7981/MT7986 boards classify WAN/LAN paths uniformly without shared DTS
   overrides.
4. Enable MTK_RSS (replacing MTK_HWLRO) in MT7981_CAPS/MT7986_CAPS, enable RXD4
   HIT_BIND_FORCE_TO_CPU sent_ppd handling on V2, extend V2 qid mark routing and
   64-queue QDMA SER save/restore (without expanding Linux netdev TX queues),
   broaden PPPQ non-WHNAT external exemption to MTK_HNAT_V2, keep HQoS IS_EXT
   fqos=1 strictly MTK_HNAT_V3-only (since NETSYS_V3 owns hqos_ext PPE_BYPASS
   recovery), and allow FROM_WED -> !IS_WHNAT IS_EXT 5G WWAN learning on V2.
5. Fix debugfs/proc buffer NUL-termination and %63s scanf bounds in hnat_debugfs.c
   and mtk_eth_dbg.c.

Signed-off-by: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
